### **d. Illustrate the concept of friend function along with an example.**  
A **friend function** is a function that is **not a member** of a class but can **access private and protected members** of that class.

**Simple C++ Example:**
```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

class Box {
private:
    int length;

public:
    Box(int l) : length(l) {}

    friend void showLength(Box b);
};

void showLength(Box b) {
    cout << "Length = " << b.length;
}

int main() {
    Box b(10);
    showLength(b);
}
```

