# **Part B**

### **2(a) Compare and contrast procedural and object-oriented programming.**

| Feature | Procedural Programming | Object-Oriented Programming |
|--------|-------------------------|------------------------------|
| Approach | Step-by-step procedures | Objects + Classes |
| Data | Exposed, not strongly protected | Encapsulated (private/protected) |
| Focus | Functions | Objects |
| Reusability | Low | High (inheritance, polymorphism) |
| Examples | C, Pascal | C++, Java, Python |

